-- R7 of specs/todo/PATTERN-REFERENCE-RULE-SPEC.md: the one diagnostic the
-- rule's own principle ("if we know enough to call it an error, we know
-- enough to correct the error") deliberately does not reach.
--
-- `amount` is a NUMBER; Deliver's second field is a Thing. Under R1 the name
-- refers, so this is a type error — and the checker cannot pick the
-- correction, because there are two and they are both plausible: the author
-- meant the reference and the action's type is wrong, or the author meant a
-- placeholder and picked a spelling that was already taken. The message
-- therefore names both.

DECLARE Thing IS ONE OF
    Widget

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Landlord
    Tenant

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Deliver HAS recipient IS AN Actor
                what IS A Thing

GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`mistyped reference` MEANS
    PARTY Tenant MUST Deliver Tenant amount WITHIN 10 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH
